  "Question": "A population contains 8 items, including 2 in a specified category. Draw 4 items without replacement. What is the mean?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "For the recorded interpretation, assume the four items are selected uniformly at random, and let \\(X\\) count the selected items in the specified category. The hypergeometric mean formula uses the population size \\(N=8\\), category count \\(K=2\\), and sample size \\(n=4\\), giving\n\\[\nE[X]=\\frac{nK}{N}=\\frac{4\\cdot2}{8}=\\frac88=1.\n\\]\nThe displayed question leaves this interpretation implicit. Without uniform sampling, a rule that always selects four noncategory items gives \\(E[X]=0\\), while a rule that always includes both category items gives \\(E[X]=2\\). Both rules select four items without replacement. Thus the answer is \\(1\\) under the recorded uniform category-count interpretation; the wording alone does not determine a unique mean.",
